WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.334 --> 00:00:01.168
Whoa.

00:00:12.304 --> 00:00:13.555
Oh my God!

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:15.349
How crazy was that fight?

00:00:16.141 --> 00:00:17.643
Flynn was so savage.

00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:19.770
Have you made out
with him yet?

00:00:20.646 --> 00:00:21.980
One, two, three…

00:00:22.064 --> 00:00:23.857
To Ellen!

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:28.153
It's still Elle,
but whatever.

00:00:28.904 --> 00:00:30.739
I'm so sorry, I forgot.

00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:32.658
I've got some karaoke,
gotta get ready.

00:00:32.741 --> 00:00:34.326
Guys, yo. Say hello to Elle.

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:37.079
Hi, Elle.

00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:38.539
Hi!

00:00:38.622 --> 00:00:41.124
-Hello, boys.
-Chloe! How are you?

00:00:41.792 --> 00:00:44.419
So, who's singing
tonight then?

00:00:44.503 --> 00:00:46.839
Oh my God!
Get dressed, naked boy.

00:00:46.922 --> 00:00:48.048
Scandalous.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:52.803
You take care of yourself.

00:00:53.637 --> 00:00:54.721
You too.

00:01:03.272 --> 00:01:04.439
For whatever it's worth…

00:01:05.858 --> 00:01:07.401
I want you to know

00:01:07.484 --> 00:01:09.862
that I think you are

00:01:09.945 --> 00:01:12.155
an absolutely
brilliant woman.

00:01:14.366 --> 00:01:15.576
Thank you, Chloe.

00:01:16.869 --> 00:01:18.704
Sorry, was my description
not vivid enough?

00:01:18.787 --> 00:01:21.039
I literally described
100 different ways

00:01:21.123 --> 00:01:22.875
Marco can get it.

00:01:28.422 --> 00:01:29.423
Awesome.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.386
I take it you're the one
from the intercom?

00:01:35.137 --> 00:01:36.013
Yeah.

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.723
But they're already
calling me

00:01:37.806 --> 00:01:40.851
the "get-it girl",
but I go by Elle.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.395
I don't know. "Get-it girl"
has a nice ring to it.

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:45.147
Cool.

00:01:45.898 --> 00:01:46.899
Well…

00:01:47.608 --> 00:01:49.985
goodbye, Elle Evans.

00:01:51.153 --> 00:01:53.947
Goodbye, MVP.

00:01:56.867 --> 00:01:57.701
Hi, guys!

00:01:58.285 --> 00:01:59.328
-Hi!
-Hey!

00:01:59.411 --> 00:02:00.954
That's Mrs Flynn.

00:02:01.038 --> 00:02:02.581
She's sort of
a surrogate mom to me.

00:02:03.165 --> 00:02:04.082
I couldn't
have made it

00:02:04.166 --> 00:02:05.834
through the years
without her.

00:02:05.918 --> 00:02:07.377
How's school going?

00:02:07.461 --> 00:02:09.379
Let's just say interesting.

00:02:09.463 --> 00:02:10.881
I don't know what
that means,

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:13.675
but I want to hear
all the gory details later.

00:02:14.885 --> 00:02:15.969
Is there a problem?

00:02:16.637 --> 00:02:17.804
Mrs Flynn?

00:02:20.557 --> 00:02:21.433
No.

00:02:21.517 --> 00:02:23.519
No problem at all.

00:02:24.436 --> 00:02:26.063
I'm just not selling
this house.

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:28.148
You'd be walking away
from millions.

00:02:28.732 --> 00:02:31.193
All of these old homes
are being taken down.

00:02:36.198 --> 00:02:37.574
Just not this one.

00:02:38.659 --> 00:02:40.077
Good day, gentlemen.

00:02:46.625 --> 00:02:47.918
-Morning!
-Morning.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.127
Morning.

00:02:50.504 --> 00:02:51.547
Elle.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:54.132
Dad, my pants ripped.
This is literally all I had.

00:02:54.216 --> 00:02:55.676
I'm gonna set up
these pieces.

00:02:55.759 --> 00:02:57.261
Good for you.

00:02:57.344 --> 00:02:58.637
He's very particular.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.931
Oh! And I call the race car.

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:04.268
Hey, Dad! Where are my
other pairs of school pants?

00:03:04.351 --> 00:03:06.019
They're at the cleaners!

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.109
I'm not disappointed
in you, Elle.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:16.572
We all make mistakes.

00:03:17.573 --> 00:03:19.074
It's what you do after

00:03:19.157 --> 00:03:21.034
that shows who you are.

00:03:31.295 --> 00:03:32.504
I guess I'm next.

00:03:51.023 --> 00:03:51.857
Whoa.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:54.610
I hope you like
what you see.

00:04:03.285 --> 00:04:04.369
Lee?

00:04:04.453 --> 00:04:05.329
Lee!

00:04:05.412 --> 00:04:07.831
Geronimo!

00:04:07.915 --> 00:04:09.166
Oh, no.

00:04:15.964 --> 00:04:19.176
Oh my God!
That was a good one!

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:20.677
That was a good one.

00:04:20.761 --> 00:04:21.678
Noah.

00:04:21.762 --> 00:04:23.430
-Hey.
-Fancy seeing you here.

00:04:23.514 --> 00:04:25.766
-What's up?
-Nice seeing you, brother.

00:04:25.849 --> 00:04:26.767
Good to see you, bro.

00:04:28.727 --> 00:04:29.853
Congratulations again.

00:04:29.937 --> 00:04:32.064
So when's the wedding?
Do you guys have a date?

00:04:32.147 --> 00:04:34.775
Yeah, we're thinking
like late May.

00:04:34.858 --> 00:04:35.859
Okay, late May.

00:04:35.943 --> 00:04:36.944
Can't wait.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:42.074
We were talking
about maybe going

00:04:42.157 --> 00:04:44.952
-and getting some churros.
-Were you now?

00:04:45.035 --> 00:04:46.912
So we'll catch up
with you guys later.

00:04:46.995 --> 00:04:48.580
-Cool, yeah.
-Good to see you, bro.

00:04:48.664 --> 00:04:50.123
Okay. Bye.

00:04:50.207 --> 00:04:52.084
Lee!
You seen my athletic cup?

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:53.585
Yes, ass-hat!

00:04:53.669 --> 00:04:55.838
I needed it
for all those varsity sports

00:04:55.921 --> 00:04:57.631
I'm constantly playing,
you know?

00:04:59.842 --> 00:05:00.676
Hey, Shelly.

00:05:00.759 --> 00:05:03.220
He knows I hate
being called Shelly.

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:04.555
Yes, Noah?

00:05:04.638 --> 00:05:07.015
I know he hates
being called Noah.

00:05:08.016 --> 00:05:10.310
Okay, well, I mean,
when I'm in town again,

00:05:10.394 --> 00:05:12.396
we should go
for a ride together.

00:05:14.398 --> 00:05:16.775
Only if you'd… like that.

00:05:17.818 --> 00:05:19.611
I would like that.
That sounds fun.

00:05:20.904 --> 00:05:21.822
Great.

00:05:23.615 --> 00:05:26.159
Well, I've got to go see
some friends

00:05:26.243 --> 00:05:29.121
-and I have an early flight.
-No, of course.

00:05:29.204 --> 00:05:30.914
But, no, no, no.
I'll call you.

00:05:30.998 --> 00:05:32.791
Sure. Yeah.
If you've got time.

00:05:33.917 --> 00:05:35.210
I've got time.

00:05:39.256 --> 00:05:40.549
-I'm gonna go.
-Okay.

00:05:40.632 --> 00:05:42.050
-Okay.
-All right.

00:05:42.134 --> 00:05:43.051
I'll see…

00:05:43.635 --> 00:05:45.095
-I'll see you later.
-Okay.

00:05:45.179 --> 00:05:46.847
See you. Okay, bye.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.098
Bye.

00:05:50.225 --> 00:05:51.894
Look at that cute baby!

00:05:51.977 --> 00:05:53.604
That's me, Elle Evans.

00:05:53.687 --> 00:05:56.023
And the smelly, less-cute
baby right next to me,

00:05:56.106 --> 00:05:57.649
that's my best friend Lee.

00:05:57.733 --> 00:06:00.569
Lee and I were born on the
same day at the same time

00:06:00.652 --> 00:06:02.779
here in Los Angeles,
California.

00:06:02.863 --> 00:06:04.323
Our moms were BFFs

00:06:04.406 --> 00:06:06.700
before people
even used the term BFF.

00:06:06.783 --> 00:06:08.368
So, we were raised
like twins

00:06:08.452 --> 00:06:11.371
and we've been pretty much
inseparable ever since.

00:06:11.455 --> 00:06:14.041
Standing there
at the carnival

00:06:14.124 --> 00:06:17.085
and seeing Noah again
after all that time…

00:06:18.795 --> 00:06:21.215
I couldn't help
but think of one thing.

00:06:31.934 --> 00:06:33.644
That all of this happened

00:06:33.727 --> 00:06:35.145
just because of…

00:06:36.021 --> 00:06:38.148
well, you know.

